<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yamanaka et al. (2023), Miao et al. (2023) & Adhyapok et al. (2021) epithelial somite rosette vertex mechanics, 3D polyhedral shell lumen pressurization and live HES7 clock-wavefront coupled mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition (MET) model — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every section banner names its law id, source figures and Lean theorem (L195-199, L415-419, L716-721, L824-830); the docstring states Laws 1-5 with their equations and theorem names (L60-105); the math KG loop file registers all five equations with Lean declarations, loci and code loci (equations 4-5 added); the Pass 3 remediation block in the docstring maps each v2 item to its section and states the reductions (L38-58). Deductions: the MESP2 median rule, the RIPPLY2 0.5 h ramp and the EphA4/ephrinB2 directional boundary rule (L975-987) cite no specific figure of Yamanaka (2023) or Morimoto-type Mesp2 work (-4); the frustum lateral-face area approximation with face-averaged radii (L570-572) is stated but not derived (-2); Law 3 (Y-27632 / Minus-Matrigel collapse) has no dedicated function: its math KG code_locus (YAML L138) points at the energy-landscape and regime-evaluator ranges where gamma_ap = gamma_bas is merely a table entry (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py L975–L987: MESP2 / RIPPLY2 / boundary rules without figure-level citations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py#L975-L987>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yamanaka et al. (2023), Miao et al. (2023) & Adhyapok et al. (2021) epithelial somite rosette vertex mechanics, 3D polyhedral shell lumen pressurization and live HES7 clock-wavefront coupled mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition (MET) model — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The 2D vertex energy and its polygon/continuum equilibrium laws (L200-379), the Eph/ephrin cleft barrier (L722-748) and the Y-27632 collapse are unchanged and faithful. Pass 3 adds a genuine 3D polyhedral shell energy with volume elasticity, three face-tension classes and a -P V_lumen term (L535-628) whose radial balance is derived (L478-533) and reproduced numerically to 1e-4, and a Lewis (2003) delayed oscillator with his published her1 kernel (a=4.5, b=c=0.23, k=33, p0=40, T_m=12, T_p=2.8 min) uniformly time-scaled (L831-883), the Cooke-Zeeman arrest law and an ephrinB2-|EphA4+ boundary rule consistent with Adhyapok (2021). Deductions: the shell cells are radial frusta with 2 DOF on a fixed Voronoi tessellation (L564-581, lateral faces L570-572), so the \"polyhedral scutoid shell\" cannot form scutoids or T1s and the audit at L687-714 reports 0 by construction (-4); the clock is synchronous (one DDE state copied to 64 cells, L950-971) so kinematic HES7 waves, Notch coupling and the posterior-anterior period gradient of axioloids are absent (-3); MESP2 / RIPPLY2 are a median-threshold and fixed-delay rule set (L975-987), not the TBX6/MESP2/RIPPLY2 network, and the tension \"coupling\" is an imposed exponential ramp of time-since-arrest (L989-1002), one-way (-3); the 3D shell is run with the 2D-fitted tensions and lands at rho_3D = 0.323 rather than 0.305 with no re-fit (-2); credited +2 for the five machine-checked Lean theorems covering every law." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-model-fidelity-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-model-fidelity-7> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yamanaka et al. (2023), Miao et al. (2023) & Adhyapok et al. (2021) epithelial somite rosette vertex mechanics, 3D polyhedral shell lumen pressurization and live HES7 clock-wavefront coupled mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition (MET) model — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` now returns 10 measurements (L1316-1447; Pass 3 list L1343-1394): the 5 Pass 2 values plus the 3D WT lumen ratio (0.3229 vs 0.305 empirical, Law 4 analytic 0.3229), rupture pressure P_crit (0.115 vs Laplace bound 0.510), HES7 period (4.995 vs 5.0 h), boundary spacing (100.0 vs v T = 99.9 um) and the oldest-somite live-coupled ratio (0.3033 vs 0.305). Deductions: three of the five new references are model-internal (Laplace bound, v T, calibration target) and the period measurement validates its own calibration, as the reference_source strings themselves say (L1359-1383) (-7); the 3D ratio misses the only empirical anchor by 6% with no stage-resolved somitocoel data digitised from Yamanaka Figs. 2-3 or Miao Fig. 4 to test the S0 -> S-III series (L1384-1393) (-3); the specimen reference 47.1429 px is the disputed scout value (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
