<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yamanaka et al. (2023), Miao et al. (2023) & Adhyapok et al. (2021) epithelial somite rosette vertex mechanics, 3D polyhedral shell lumen pressurization and live HES7 clock-wavefront coupled mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition (MET) model — MorphoEval overall 89.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 post-remediation evaluation of `2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py` (89.7/100, down from 91.7 in Pass 2). Both v2 remediation items are closed in reduced, explicitly disclosed form: Section 2b adds a closed 3D polyhedral shell of 96 spherical-Voronoi frustum cells with an explicit somitecoel pressure term, relaxed over 192 radial degrees of freedom and reproducing the new closed-form Law 4 balance to 1e-4 (WT rho_3D = 0.3229 vs 0.305 empirical; Y-27632 0.7098), a pressure sweep with a saddle-node rupture pressure P_crit = 0.115 gamma_lat/um below the Laplace bound 0.510, and a scutoid audit that honestly reports 0 scutoids by construction; Section 3b runs a Lewis (2003) HES7 delayed oscillator calibrated to the human 5 h period in every PSM cell, arrests it with a Cooke-Zeeman wavefront, gates MESP2/RIPPLY2 and boundary fixation on the frozen phase, and feeds exponential RhoA/ROCK and EphA4/ephrinB2 tension ramps live into the vertex, shell and cleft models (S = 100 um = v T; S0 0.343 -> S-III 0.303 maturation; Y-27632 and Eph/ephrin knockdown controls). Two Lean 4 theorems (`yamanaka_2023_shell_lumen_pressurization`, `hes7_wavefront_arrest_tension_gradient`) bring the file to 5 theorems with 0 sorrys; the reference JSON is now SHA-256 pinned; 10 measurements; PNG, clock PNG and GIF regenerate byte-identically. The score falls because the round surfaced defects v2 had scored past: the new measurements lean on model-internal references, the 3D shell was not re-calibrated and misses 0.305 by 6%, the specimen rosette_metrics in the vendored JSON contradict the script's own segmentation (CV 0.2010 vs 0.2391; v2 quoted the JSON), the clock is synchronous and the MESP2/RIPPLY2 logic is a threshold rule set. Overall 89.7/100 (faithfulness 88.4, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/somitoid_chirality_buckling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py at d58a084, image/png, 1160191 B, 2505×2298 px, artifact_sha256 8d4112473f06311e45765334cca5fb587c718ffbf4fb1a76b844ea598e7313e6 (sha256 8d4112473f06311e45765334cca5fb587c718ffbf4fb1a76b844ea598e7313e6), spec_fingerprint c1110cb9038d37a536b327b4b7e47002f40a93acd13d457cf0444c105660f6c4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c1110cb9038d37a536b327b4b7e47002f40a93acd13d457cf0444c105660f6c4; artifact_sha256: 8d4112473f06311e45765334cca5fb587c718ffbf4fb1a76b844ea598e7313e6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/somitoid_chirality_buckling/scout_manifest.json=8326704c93aa8a75..., datasets/somitoid_chirality_buckling/somitoid_chirality_buckling_reference.json=72127bb5b83f59d0..., datasets/somitoid_chirality_buckling/somitoid_rosette_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-somitoid-chirality-buckling-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Yamanaka et al. (2023) Nature 614:509-520 & Miao et al. (2023) Nature 614:500-508: Matrigel ECM embedding and RhoA/ROCK-dependent apical actomyosin constriction drive epithelial somite rosette polarization and central somitecoel lumen formation in human axioloids and somitoids; HES7 oscillations and periodic MESP2/RIPPLY2 stripes precede boundary formation | Adhyapok et al. (2021) Dev. Cell 56:1312-1324: combined apical constriction (gamma_ap > gamma_bas) and EphA4/ephrinB2 heterotypic boundary repulsion (gamma_het > gamma_hom) govern somite rounding and inter-somitic cleft separation | Y-27632 ROCK inhibition or absence of Matrigel abolishes the apico-basal tension differential and prevents polarized epithelial somite rosette morphogenesis | Lewis (2003): a transcriptional-delay autoinhibition loop yields a limit-cycle segmentation oscillator; Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) and Matsuda et al. (2020): the human iPSC-PSM HES7 period is ~5 h | Cooke & Zeeman (1976): segment length equals wavefront speed times clock period, S = v T | Gomez-Galvez et al. (2018): scutoids arise from apical/basal Voronoi mismatch under anisotropic (tubular) curvature; a spherical epithelium predicts none; reconstructed_in_script: 2D 32-vertex apico-basal differential interfacial tension relaxation solver for an N=16 wedge-cell somite rosette (WT L_ap/L_bas = 0.3030 vs 0.3030 polygon law, 0.305 empirical), 6-regime perturbation series (Pearson r = 0.9989, RMSE = 0.0154), Eph/ephrin cleft barrier (S_cleft = 0.8189 WT vs 0.0930 KD), 28x28 phase diagram and bilateral specimen segmentation (45.375 px, CV 0.2391) carried from Pass 2 | Pass 3: closed 3D polyhedral shell of 96 spherical-Voronoi frustum cells with volume elasticity, face tensions and -P V_lumen, relaxed over 192 radii and matched to the closed-form Law 4 balance (WT rho_3D = 0.3229 discrete vs 0.3229 analytic; Y-27632 0.7098), a lumen-pressure sweep with saddle-node rupture P_crit = 0.115 gamma_lat/um (Laplace open-shell bound 0.510) and a scutoid topology audit (0 scutoids by construction) | Pass 3: Lewis (2003) HES7 delayed oscillator time-scaled to T = 4.995 h in 64 PSM cells, Cooke-Zeeman wavefront arrest (v = 20 um/h), MESP2 gated by frozen HES7 phase (0.50 of each segment), RIPPLY2 boundary fixation, 5 ephrinB2-|EphA4+ boundaries at S = 100.0 um = v T, exponential RhoA/ROCK gamma_ap(x,t) (tau 3 h) and EphA4/ephrinB2 gamma_het,k(t) (tau 1.5 h) ramps fed live into the vertex, shell and cleft models: S0 0.3428 -> S-III 0.3033 maturation, Y-27632 coupled 0.7013 at every stage, Eph/ephrin KD cleft 0.0930; transfer_boundary: The 2D and 3D laws share the same empirical cross-section ratio 0.305 as their only external anchor; the 3D shell with the 2D-fitted tensions gives 0.323 (6% high) and the tensions were NOT re-fitted for 3D | The clock-coupling constants v, tau_ROCK, tau_Eph, tau_RIPPLY2 are model choices (segment ~100 um, MET over ~1 period); S = v T is therefore an analytical identity check, not a comparison with a digitised somite length; the HES7 period is calibrated to 5 h, so its measurement validates the calibration rather than predicting the period | The HES7 clock is synchronous across the PSM (Cooke-Zeeman limit): no posterior-anterior period gradient, hence no kinematic HES7 waves as seen in axioloids; the coupling is one-way (clock -> tension), with no mechanical feedback on the clock or on MESP2 | The 3D shell cells are radial frusta with 2 DOF each on a fixed Voronoi tessellation: no tangential vertex motion, no T1 transitions, no scutoids; the 0% scutoid result is a construction, consistent with but not a test of Gomez-Galvez (2018) | No somitocoel pressure has been measured in the source papers; P_crit is referenced to the model-internal Laplace bound only; does_not_claim: Full 3D sclerotome/dermomyotome lineage regionalization, scutoid or T1 cell rearrangements, kinematic HES7 phase waves, Notch-mediated clock synchronisation, a TBX6/MESP2/RIPPLY2 gene-network model, mechanical feedback onto the clock, or a quantitative match of the stage-resolved lumen ratios to digitised Yamanaka (2023) / Miao (2023) stage data." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py:1349, 1389 and 1384-1393 — the 3D WT shell gives rho_3D = 0.323 against the single empirical anchor 0.305 (6% high) with the 2D-fitted tensions and no re-fit, and the S0 -> S-III maturation series has no digitised stage data to compare against. Re-fit gamma_ap / gamma_bas for the 3D law (or report the fitted values alongside the 2D ones) and digitise stage-resolved somitocoel / somite radii from Yamanaka 2023 Figs. 2-3 or Miao 2023 Fig. 4.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py:1359-1383 — three of the five Pass 3 measurements reference model-internal values (Laplace bound, v T, calibration target) and the HES7-period measurement validates its own calibration. Replace at least two with external references (e.g. digitised somitoid segment length from Miao 2023 / Sanaki-Matsumiya 2022; HES7 period from a non-calibrated prediction such as the Lewis period formula) or label them `derived_from: model-internal` in the measurement schema.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py:153-159 and 989-1002 — v = 20 um/h, tau_ROCK = 3 h, tau_Eph = 1.5 h and tau_RIPPLY2 = 1 h are hand-chosen and the gamma_ap / gamma_het \"coupling\" is an imposed exponential of time-since-arrest with no feedback. Digitise MET timing (pMLC2 / ZO-1 / F-actin apical enrichment vs somite stage) from Yamanaka 2023 Fig. 3 / Extended Data and Miao 2023 Fig. 4, fit tau_ROCK and v, and sweep them.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py:2200 — the self-test accepts |rho_3D - 0.305| < 0.03, which passes the 6% miss; tighten after the 3D re-fit, and add a requirements lock (python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0) so the byte-identical render claim is pinned to an environment.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py:535-628 and 687-714 — shell cells are radial frusta with 2 DOF on a fixed Voronoi tessellation; scutoids / T1 transitions are impossible, so the \"0 scutoids\" result is a construction. Free the apical and basal Voronoi vertex positions independently (true 3D vertex model) or add anisotropic (tubular) curvature so Gomez-Galvez (2018) scutoid formation can be tested rather than assumed.",
        "remediation needed: 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py:950-971 — the HES7 oscillator is one DDE state copied to all 64 PSM cells (synchronous Cooke-Zeeman clock), so the kinematic HES7 waves of axioloids (Yamanaka 2023 Fig. 1; Diaz-Cuadros 2020) are absent and the arrested phase depends only on x/v. Add a posterior-anterior period gradient (FGF-dependent delay or degradation rate) so waves travel and arrest at wave arrival, and compare the wave number per PSM length to the papers' kymographs.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/somitoid_chirality_buckling/somitoid_chirality_buckling_reference.json:71-80 vs 2021-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.py:1223-1275 — scout rosette_metrics (lower 8, 47.1429 px, CV 0.2010) contradict the script's segmentation (lower 10, 45.375 px, CV 0.2391); v2 quoted the JSON. Re-count the rosettes manually on the specimen, record the method, and make the JSON and the script agree (or carry both with uncertainty).",
        "remediation needed: morphoeval/math_kg_loops/yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling.yaml:74-228 — the five `code_locus` ranges were refreshed by hand in Pass 3 and will drift again; add a self-test (or a build check) that resolves each `code_locus` / `lean_locus` to the named function or theorem so stale loci fail loudly." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.97e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yamanaka et al. (2023), Miao et al. (2023) & Adhyapok et al. (2021) epithelial somite rosette vertex mechanics, 3D polyhedral shell lumen pressurization and live HES7 clock-wavefront coupled mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition (MET) model — Parameter expressivity: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The 6-regime series and 28x28 (gamma_ap, Matrigel %) phase diagram remain (L750-822, L1127-1164). Pass 3 adds a 25-point lumen-pressure sweep with monotone rho_3D(P) and a located rupture pressure, checked at 3 pressures against the discrete shell (L630-685, Panel H), a stage axis (S0 -> S-III) along which the live gamma_ap ramp visibly tightens the rosette (L1065-1112, clock PNG panel d), and coupled Y-27632 and Eph/ephrin knockdown controls that leave the boundary count unchanged while abolishing MET or clefting (L2226-2236). Deductions: the clock constants v, tau_ROCK, tau_Eph, tau_RIPPLY2 and the shell constants N_3D, V_0, K_V are fixed (L148-159) and never swept, so the sensitivity of S, P_crit and the maturation time to them is unshown (-5); the only period control is the calibration target (-3)." ;
