<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-yaman-somitoid-chirality-buckling-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yamanaka et al. (2023), Miao et al. (2023) & Adhyapok et al. (2021) epithelial somite rosette vertex mechanics, 3D polyhedral shell lumen pressurization and live HES7 clock-wavefront coupled mesenchymal-to-epithelial transition (MET) model — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic throughout: Fibonacci-sphere seeds and explicit-Euler DDE need no RNG; the 2D and 3D relaxations use fixed seeds and both are asserted bitwise two-run identical (L2167-2172, L2193-2197); two consecutive default renders of the PNG, clock PNG and GIF were byte-identical (SHA-256 8d411247..., dc46f670..., 5d678180...). `--self-test` runs 6 check groups covering SHA-256 integrity, both solvers, the pressure sweep, the scutoid audit, period calibration, S = v T, MESP2 half-segments, the AP maturation gradient and the two coupled controls, then all 10 measurements, in ~5.6 s; the default render takes ~7 s (L2154-2266). Deductions: no requirements lock file pins this script's environment (versions are recorded only in this audit) (-4); the self-test tolerance for the 3D WT ratio vs 0.305 is 0.03, wide enough to pass a 6% miss (L2200) (-2); matplotlib writes a font cache outside the repo unless MPLCONFIGDIR is set (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
